IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-interpretation`

-- Tests for sg-interpretation.l4 (s 4 outside the defined terms). Expected values are worked out by hand from the subsection named beside each assertion.

§ `Section 4(1): the opening words`

-- Columns: the word is one subsection (1) defines; a contrary intention appears.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the definition in subsection (1) governs the word where it is used` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the definition in subsection (1) governs the word where it is used` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A word that subsection (1) does not define: the opening words say nothing of it.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the definition in subsection (1) governs the word where it is used` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the definition in subsection (1) governs the word where it is used` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 4(3): when a statement is untrue`

-- Columns: included in a statement in lieu of prospectus; misleading in the form and context in which it is included.
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the statement is deemed to be untrue` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the statement is deemed to be untrue` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the statement is deemed to be untrue` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the statement is deemed to be untrue` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 4(4): when a statement is included in a statement in lieu of prospectus`

-- Columns: contained in a report or memorandum; appears on the face; incorporated by reference; issued with it.
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the statement is deemed to be included in a statement in lieu of prospectus` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the statement is deemed to be included in a statement in lieu of prospectus` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the statement is deemed to be included in a statement in lieu of prospectus` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The report has none of the three connections: not deemed included.
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the statement is deemed to be included in a statement in lieu of prospectus` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The connection without the statement being in the report: not deemed included.
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the statement is deemed to be included in a statement in lieu of prospectus` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 4(5): the invitation to deposit or lend`

-- Columns: an invitation to the public to deposit money with or lend money to a corporation; the corporation is a prescribed entity mentioned in s 239(4) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001.
#ASSERT `s 4(5) the invitation is deemed to be an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures of the corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(5) the invitation is deemed to be an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures of the corporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Some other invitation: the subsection says nothing of it (not "no").
#ASSERT `s 4(5) the invitation is deemed to be an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures of the corporation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(5) the invitation is deemed to be an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures of the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 4(5A): the document deemed a debenture`

-- Columns: issued, or intended or required to be issued, by a corporation; acknowledges its indebtedness; for money deposited or lent in response to a (5) invitation.
#ASSERT `s 4(5A) the document is deemed to be a debenture` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(5A) the document is deemed to be a debenture` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(5A) the document is deemed to be a debenture` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(5A) the document is deemed to be a debenture` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 4(7): references to bankruptcy`

-- Columns: a contrary intention appears; the person is in the situation the reference covers.
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a person being or becoming bankrupt covers the person being or becoming insolvent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a person being or becoming bankrupt covers the person being or becoming insolvent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a person being or becoming bankrupt covers the person being or becoming insolvent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a person assigning the person's estate for the benefit of creditors or making an arrangement with them covers the same under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a person assigning the person's estate for the benefit of creditors or making an arrangement with them covers the same under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a person assigning the person's estate for the benefit of creditors or making an arrangement with them covers the same under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a person being an undischarged bankrupt covers the person being an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a person being an undischarged bankrupt covers the person being an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a person being an undischarged bankrupt covers the person being an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a status, condition, act, matter or thing under the law of bankruptcy covers the corresponding one under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a status, condition, act, matter or thing under the law of bankruptcy covers the corresponding one under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(7) a reference to a status, condition, act, matter or thing under the law of bankruptcy covers the corresponding one under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 4(8): the affairs of a corporation`

-- The paragraphs. Columns after the matter: the corporation is a trustee but not a trustee corporation; the act was done at one of the four times in (d); the corporation has issued interests.
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(a) the promotion, formation, membership, control, business, trading, transactions, dealings, property, liabilities, profits, income, receipts, losses, outgoings or expenditure of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) only for a corporation that is a trustee and not a trustee corporation.
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(b) the identity of the beneficiaries under a trust of which the corporation is trustee, their rights and the payments they have received or are entitled to receive` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(b) the identity of the beneficiaries under a trust of which the corporation is trustee, their rights and the payments they have received or are entitled to receive` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(c) the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d) the act done at one of the four times; the conduct of those office-holders is in without condition.
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(d) an act or thing done by or on behalf of the corporation, or to or in relation to it or its business or property, at a time when it was in receivership, under judicial management, administering a compromise or arrangement, or being wound up` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(d) an act or thing done by or on behalf of the corporation, or to or in relation to it or its business or property, at a time when it was in receivership, under judicial management, administering a compromise or arrangement, or being wound up` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(d) the conduct of a receiver, a receiver and manager, a judicial manager, a person administering a compromise or arrangement, a liquidator or a provisional liquidator of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(e) the ownership of shares in, debentures of, and interests issued by, the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(f) the power of persons to exercise, or to control the exercise of, voting rights attached to shares in the corporation or to dispose of, or to control the disposal of, such shares` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(g) the ascertainment of the persons who are or have been financially interested in the success or failure of the corporation or able to control or materially influence its policy` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(h) the circumstances under which a person acquired or disposed of, or became entitled to acquire or dispose of, shares in, debentures of, or interests issued by, the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (i) only where the corporation has issued interests.
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(i) the financial or business undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or investment contract to which interests issued by the corporation relate` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(i) the financial or business undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or investment contract to which interests issued by the corporation relate` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8)(j) the audit of, or working papers or reports of an auditor concerning, a matter referred to in paragraphs (a) to (i)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The list is open ("including a reference to").
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` `s 4(8) some other matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The reference must be in one of the named provisions; a contrary intention displaces the list.
-- Columns: the reference is in section 8A, 8C, 8D, 216, Part 9 or section 402; a contrary intention appears; the matter; the three conditions.
#ASSERT `s 4(8) a reference to the affairs of a corporation covers the matter` TRUE FALSE `s 4(8)(c) the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(8) a reference to the affairs of a corporation covers the matter` FALSE FALSE `s 4(8)(c) the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(8) a reference to the affairs of a corporation covers the matter` TRUE TRUE `s 4(8)(c) the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(8) a reference to the affairs of a corporation covers the matter` TRUE FALSE `s 4(8) some other matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 4(9): the affairs of a company or a foreign company`

-- Columns: the reference is to the affairs of a company or foreign company; the matter; the three conditions as in (8).
-- (9) carries no "unless the contrary intention appears" and no list of sections.
#ASSERT `s 4(9) a reference to the affairs of a company or a foreign company covers the matter` TRUE `s 4(8)(e) the ownership of shares in, debentures of, and interests issued by, the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(9) a reference to the affairs of a company or a foreign company covers the matter` TRUE `s 4(8)(i) the financial or business undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or investment contract to which interests issued by the corporation relate` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(9) a reference to the affairs of a company or a foreign company covers the matter` FALSE `s 4(8)(e) the ownership of shares in, debentures of, and interests issued by, the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 4(10) and (11): a company with one director`

#ASSERT `s 4(10) a reference to the directors of the company is a reference to its only director` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(10) a reference to the directors of the company is a reference to its only director` 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(10) a reference to the directors of the company is a reference to its only director` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Columns: the number of directors; the act has been done by the only director.
#ASSERT `s 4(11) the act of the only director counts as the doing of the act by 2 or more directors` 1 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(11) the act of the only director counts as the doing of the act by 2 or more directors` 1 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(11) the act of the only director counts as the doing of the act by 2 or more directors` 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(11) the act of the only director counts as the doing of the act by 2 or more directors` 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 4(12): the Minister of State`

-- Columns: the provision where the reference to the Minister appears; a Minister of State for the Minister's Ministry; authorised by the Minister to hear the appeal.
#ASSERT `s 4(12) the reference to the Minister includes the Minister of State` "20(3)" TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(12) the reference to the Minister includes the Minister of State` "378(16)" TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE         -- the last in the list
#ASSERT `s 4(12) the reference to the Minister includes the Minister of State` "27(12C)" TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(12) the reference to the Minister includes the Minister of State` "20(3)" TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING             -- not authorised
#ASSERT `s 4(12) the reference to the Minister includes the Minister of State` "20(3)" FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING             -- not a Minister of State
-- A provision the subsection does not list.
#ASSERT `s 4(12) the reference to the Minister includes the Minister of State` "20(4)" TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(12) the reference to the Minister includes the Minister of State` "378(10)" TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD 1) `s 4(12) the provisions in which a Minister of State may stand for the Minister`) EQUALS 19

§ `Section 4(13): the memorandum and articles become the constitution`

-- Columns: the date asked; the memorandum and articles were in force immediately before 3 January 2016.
#ASSERT `s 4(13)(a)(i) the memorandum and articles in force immediately before 3 January 2016 are deemed to be the company's constitution` (Date 3 1 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE         -- the day it takes effect
#ASSERT `s 4(13)(a)(i) the memorandum and articles in force immediately before 3 January 2016 are deemed to be the company's constitution` (Date 2 1 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE           -- the day before
#ASSERT `s 4(13)(a)(i) the memorandum and articles in force immediately before 3 January 2016 are deemed to be the company's constitution` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(13)(a)(i) the memorandum and articles in force immediately before 3 January 2016 are deemed to be the company's constitution` (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(13)(a)(i) the memorandum and articles in force immediately before 3 January 2016 are deemed to be the company's constitution` (Date 2 1 2016) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE           -- before the day: no, whatever was in force
#ASSERT `s 4(13)(a)(ii) the company may amend the memorandum and articles in the same manner as a constitution` (Date 3 1 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(13)(a)(ii) the company may amend the memorandum and articles in the same manner as a constitution` (Date 2 1 2016) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(13)(a)(ii) the company may amend the memorandum and articles in the same manner as a constitution` (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Columns: the date asked; the reference is in a written law, or in a contract or other document having legal effect.
#ASSERT `s 4(13)(b) a reference to the memorandum or articles of association is deemed to refer to the company's constitution` (Date 3 1 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(13)(b) a reference to the memorandum or articles of association is deemed to refer to the company's constitution` (Date 2 1 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(13)(b) a reference to the memorandum or articles of association is deemed to refer to the company's constitution` (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
